            <ArticleTitle>Efficiency of discography followed by chemonucleolysis in the treatment of sciatica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One hundred and twenty-eight patients underwent discography in our department over a period of 3 years. Eighty-four of them were treated by chemonucleolysis. All the patients were punctured by a postero-lateral approach of the intervertebral disc under fluoroscopy. Although several contraindications to chemonucleolysis are known, in our study, only one case of spondylodiscitis was noted. Overall success rate was 72.6%. Twenty-three patients (27.4%) experienced similar or increased pain after treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
